- In Linux command to see the process -> ps top 
					              htop 
						  -ef


%CPU - CPU utilization
%MEM - Memory utilization 
VSZ - virtual memory Size 
RSS:
Resident Set Size, the amount of physical memory the process is using (in kilobytes).
STAT:
The process state:
S: Sleeping.
s: A session leader.
These states provide information about what the process is doing.
START:
The time or date when the process was started.
TIME:
The amount of CPU time consumed by the process since it started.
COMMAND:
The command that was used to start the process, showing its path or executable name (e.g., /sh).

ps -ef 
uid - user id 
pid - process id and its unique no process are repeated 
proc file has the process stored 
ppid - parent process id 
       - 0 is the main process like it happens in the boot process 


- parent process and child process 
	The parents starts the child process 
C:
CPU utilization of the process (as a percentage or load factor).
STIME:
The start time of the process, indicating when the process was started (e.g., 15:26 in this image).
TTY:
The terminal associated with the process. A ? here indicates that the process is not attached to any terminal (e.g., system services or background processes).
TIME:
The amount of CPU time the process has used since it started.

pstree -p shows process id and tree version 

Types of Process 
1. Interactive - Direct user Input 
		Short level
2. Batch - Scheduling Process that is being used 
		Backup -> Database Backup
		Log Rotation 
3. Demon - any process that is in background 
	every demon process is backgroud 
	if the tty is ? then its not associated to any terminal but runs in background 
	
4. Real Time Process - Time Constarint is required 
			 crucial process needs immediate resources 

Process States
1) Running(R) - Currently running on CPU
2) Sleeping (S)
3) Zombie (Z) - Waiting for acknologment from parent process
	The process of itself is done and just waiting 
4) Idel (I) - got a interrupt

	      Waiting to be Executed 
		It has not completed its process 

5) Orphan(
6) Stopped(T) - !Running
		ended, Terminated 









	


